  "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the phrase \"it is composite or prime\" as the equivalent phrase \"it is composite or it is prime.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$y$ is composite, or it is composite or it is prime.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$y$ is composite or it is composite, or it is prime.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$y$ is composite or it is composite\" to just \"$y$ is composite.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$y$ is composite, or it is prime.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely as\n\n\"$y$ is composite or prime.\"",
